WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:05.150
In a few hours time, Meng Wanzhou will find
out whether she'll be extradited to the United

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:08.500
States ... or set free.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:12.940
Canada's arrest of one of the highest ranking
executives at Huawei has placed the country

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:18.380
in the middle of a complicated dipsute between
the U-S and China.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:25.180
I can assure everyone that we are a country
of an independent judiciary and the appropriate

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:31.500
authorities took the decisions in this case
without any political involvement or interference

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.050
as must be the case.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:38.750
But political involvement from WASHINGTON
is EXACTLY what many in China suspect is behind

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:43.710
Meng's arrest:
China's economy is becoming stronger and I

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:47.640
think the United States is unhappy about that
so they've done something to harm China's

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:48.640
interests.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:54.070
I think Meng's arrest's could be related to
that.

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:58.600
Meng was reportedly arrested on the same day
that Chinese leader Xi JinPing dined with

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:04.180
US President Donald Trump at last weekend's
G20 summit in Argentina.

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:07.601
That meeting resulted in the announcement
of a 90-day truce in their trade dispute.

00:01:07.601 --> 00:04:20.910
It is now appears to be on shakier ground
than ever.

